
# Leave tunnel mode and delete the resolver's route while the plugin's files still exist (spec 3.7); the removal
# marker keeps every later evaluation stopped until the files are gone (or an upgrade's post-install deletes it).
# This runs on an upgrade too: between the old files' removal and the new install a filter reload renders without
# the plugin's rules, so tunnel mode must not outlive the old package. A stop that cannot restore Unbound's
# forwarders restarts Unbound onto its configured root zone; when that fails too, the plugin's route becomes a
# reject route (never deleted, so no query leaves by the default route) and an error names the remedy. remove then
# reloads the filter and restarts cron through configd, else core's own scripts. The || true stays: pkg must not be
# left half-way by a removal that failed, and the plugin log says what remove could not do.
/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/OPNsense/UnboundUpstream/evaluate.php remove || true
